    "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/",
    "language": "English",
    "original_prompt": "One-Line Premise\n\nStranded on a living, hyper-adaptive planet and infected by a ravenous native parasite, a crashed pilot must constantly scavenge for life-saving medical supplies while traversing a grotesque biological nightmare to reach an abandoned xenobiology station for a cure.\n\nPlot Summary\n\nFlight Officer Kaelen wakes up in the shattered remains of the star-freighter Icarus. The sky above is a bruising purple, and the ground beneath the wreckage is not dirt, but a pulsating, fleshy membrane. Kaelen is marooned on Proxima-9, a designated 'Quarantine Class-X' death world. Worse, during the crash, a jagged piece of local bio-matter embedded itself in Kaelen's side, introducing a horrific native parasite into his bloodstream. This organism continuously consumes his vitality, forcing him into a desperate, constant search for old human med-stims or healing alien flora just to stay alive. The ship’s long-range comms are vaporized, leaving only one hope: Outpost Tartarus, an automated research station 40 miles away containing an auto-doc and a subspace transmitter.\n\nThe journey is a nightmare of survival against a hyper-adaptive ecosystem. Proxima-9 doesn't just host life; the planet itself is a single, grotesque super-organism. Kaelen must navigate canyons of calcified bone and bioluminescent carnivorous forests while managing his rapidly decaying health. Every step costs energy; every turn the parasite feeds. To survive, Kaelen must scavenge dangerous flora to power ancient tech, brew makeshift healthpacks from alien glands, and uncover the dark truth of why Outpost Tartarus went permanently offline. Time is running out before the planet's immune system fully activates, or the parasite eats him from the inside out.\n\nCore Pillars\n\nGenre: Sci-Fi / Body Horror / Survival\nTone: Oppressive, visceral, desperate.\nPlayer Role: A desperate, infected pilot relying on scavenged tech, sheer willpower, and constant medication.\nMain Conflict: Managing a relentlessly draining health pool while surviving the planet's escalating \"immune response\".\nAntagonistic Force: The internal parasite, the planet itself (The Over-Mind), and environmental hazards.\nDistinctive World Rules:\n\nParasitic Drain: The parasite drains health every turn. The player must aggressively explore to find med-packs or craft organic healing salves to survive the journey.\n\nBiological Weaponry: Traditional tech fails rapidly; the player must graft or use alien bio-tech to survive.\n\nReactive Ecosystem: High noise or violent actions cause the environment to mutate and spawn hunters.\nKey Locations: The Crash Crater, The Calcified Canyons, The Whispering Mycelium Forest, Outpost Tartarus.\nFactions: The Planet's Immune Drones (feral predators), The Assimilated (grotesque amalgamations of former humans/animals), The Station's Rogue AI.\nSignature NPC Ideas: \"Subject Zero,\" a half-assimilated researcher clinging to humanity who communicates via intercepted radio static and trades rare med-stims for scavenged tech.\nMain Quest Seeds: Formulate a potent enough temporary suppressant to survive the toxic spore-storms; breach the quarantine seals of Outpost Tartarus; use the auto-doc to surgically extract the parasite.\nSide Quest Seeds: Hunt specific multi-limbed prey to harvest their regenerative glands for powerful healthpacks; map the underground vein-tunnels to bypass surface combat.\nWin Condition: Extract the parasite in the med-bay, successfully broadcast the SOS signal, and enter cryogenic stasis inside the station's heavily armored panic room.\nLose Condition: Health reaches zero from the parasitic drain, resulting in Kaelen becoming just another grotesque creature in the hive mind.\n\nWhy It Works:\n\nRelentless Ticking Clock: The constant health drain creates an intense, anxiety-inducing gameplay loop where every movement and action must be weighed against survival resources.\n\nVisceral Atmosphere: The body-horror elements create a uniquely disturbing and memorable setting compared to sterile sci-fi.\n\nSystemic Gameplay: The \"reactive ecosystem\" rule combined with the need to hunt for healing items forces players into high-risk, high-reward situations.\n\nThe Geometry of Madness",
    "image_url": "assets/crashed-on-proxima-9-argo-9e896erg_cover_36e3528c.jpg",
