    "plot": "Flight Officer Kaelen awakens in the shattered escape pod of the freighter Icarus on Proxima-9, a Quarantine Class-X super-organism planet. A ravenous native parasite embedded in his side drains his vitality every turn. To survive, Kaelen must scavenge med-stims and harvest alien regenerative glands while navigating calcified bone canyons, a whispering mycelium forest, and subterranean vein-tunnels. He must brew a Spore Suppressant to survive the lethal Spore Choke, trade with the half-assimilated researcher Subject Zero, breach the quarantine seals of Outpost Tartarus, defeat the Rogue Caretaker AI, extract the parasite in the Auto-Doc Chamber, broadcast an SOS from the Subspace Comms Tower, and seal himself inside the Cryo Panic Room before his health hits zero.",
    "rules": "1. PARASITIC DRAIN: Until the parasite is surgically extracted in the Auto-Doc Chamber, the parasite drains 2 HP at the end of every turn via event script. 2. SCAVENGING & BIO-CRAFTING: Players must actively explore containers, harvest regenerative glands, and craft medical supplies to offset the drain. 3. DETERMINISTIC LOCKS & SWITCHES: Locked containers, quarantine gates, and station systems require discovered codes, keycards, or switch activations.",
    "intro_text": "Alarms warble and die in a choke of acrid smoke as you claw yourself free from the harness of the shattered escape pod. Through the cracked viewport, the sky of Proxima-9 bruises a deep,throbbing violet, and the ground outside the torn hull is not stone or soil, but a glistening, rhythmic membrane of living flesh.\n\nA white-hot spasm lances through your left ribcage. Beneath your torn flight jacket, a jagged shard of calcified alien bio-matter has fused with your skin, pumping dark, bioluminescent tendrils into your bloodstream. You can feel the organism feeding on your vitality with every heartbeat. With the Icarus destroyed, your only hope of survival lies forty miles north at Outpost Tartarus—if you can scavenge enough medical supplies here in the pod to stay alive.",
